    "type": "question",
    "label": "47",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following algebraic fractions.\n$$\\frac{\\dfrac1{x-1}+\\dfrac1{x+1}}{1+\\dfrac1{x^2-1}}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac2x$, $x\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{-1,0,1\\}$.",
      "worked": "Multiply top and bottom by $x^2-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\frac1{x-1}+\\frac1{x+1}}{1+\\frac1{x^2-1}}&=\\frac{(x+1)+(x-1)}{x^2-1+1}\\\\\\frac{\\frac1{x-1}+\\frac1{x+1}}{1+\\frac1{x^2-1}}&=\\frac{2x}{x^2}\\\\\\frac{\\frac1{x-1}+\\frac1{x+1}}{1+\\frac1{x^2-1}}&=\\frac2x\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: $x\\in\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{-1,0,1\\}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
